  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(5x-4)+2.$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(5x-4)+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(5x-4)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x-4)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(5x-4)}^{2}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{1+{(5x-4)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
